Nethack has one annoying problem, which makes itself most evident in
the character of the knight.  Whether one wears nothing, or incredibly
bulky gray dragon scale mail, the ability to hit (dexterity) and 
strength of that hit (strength) are not changed.  This is unrealistic,
and, in the case of the knight, unfair.  The knight begins with a nice
array of armor, which is mostly worthless.  Presumably, a knight's stats
suck because it's wearing all that armor.  However, if a knight strips naked,
he still fights worse than a tourist.  In actuality, a knight should have 
stats more like a barbarian's than a tourist's.  If armor is 'bulky', there
should be an invisible hit modifier, not some lame character adjustment.
Adjusting a character to match the presumed armor is a lame fix for a "real-
world" consideration.

